From anthonyb at ichr.uwa.edu.au  Mon Jun 28 08:47:53 2004
From: anthonyb at ichr.uwa.edu.au (Anthony Bosco)
Date: Mon Jun 28 08:48:05 2004
Subject: [BioC] Filtering by fold change
In-Reply-To: <200406272119.33225.peter.robinson@t-online.de>
References: <200406272119.33225.peter.robinson@t-online.de>
Message-ID: <f05111a04bd056dd2f7af@[10.0.5.134]>

The easiet way is as follows for Affymetrix data.

Load and analyse data

data<-ReadAffy()

eset<-rma(data)

exp<-eset@exprs

Calculate fold change (m) values for 2 chips

m<-exp[,1]-exp[,1]

Ask for top up and down regulated genes

X<-names(m[abs(m)>2])

Keep adjusting m cut off (ie 2 in above example) to get desired number of genes

Filter data

exp.subset<-exp[X,]

Alternatively Sort on fold change

m.sort <- sort(m,dec=T)
top.genes <- m.sort[1:1000]

exp.subset<-exp[top.genes,]


Cheers


Anthony





